      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The French position was not just about maintaining power, but also about the concept of \"mission civilisatrice\" (civilizing mission), which held that France had a moral obligation to bring modernity, democracy, and Western values to the \"backward\" and \"savage\" Algerian people. This ideology was deeply rooted in French colonialism and was used to justify the French presence in Algeria. However, this argument was largely discredited by the Algerian people and the international community, who saw it as a thinly veiled attempt to impose French dominance and suppress Algerian culture.",
